C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Water Resources Systems Analysis
      Example Coups Minivans from Lecture Example 2 
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      An irrigated farm can be planted in two crops:  eggplants and tomatoes.  Data are as fol-lows:
       
      Seasonal Resource
      Inputs or Profit        Crops        Resource
      Availability
              Eggplant        Tomatoes
      Water        1x103 gal/plant        2x103 gal/plant      4x106 gal/year
      Land        4 ft2/plant        3 ft2/plant               1.2x104 ft2
      Labor         5hr/plant        2.5/hr plant              17,500 hours
      Profit/plant        $6        $7
       
                      Determine the optimal planting for the two crops.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      David E Rosenberg
      david.rosenberg@usu.edu
      September 15, 2015
  27   
  28  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  29  SETS vehicles Type of vehicle to produce /Coup, Minivan/
  30       res resources /Metal, CircuitBoards, Labor/;
  31   
  32  * 2. DEFINE input data
  33  PARAMETERS
  34     c(vehicles) Objective function coefficients ($ per vehicle)
  35           /Coup 6000,
  36          Minivan 7000 /
  37   
  38     b(res) Right hand constraint values (per resource)
  39            /Metal 4000000,
  40             CircuitBoards  12000,
  41             Labor  17500/;
  42   
  43  TABLE A(vehicles,res) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  44                   Metal    CircuitBoards   Labor
  45   Coup           1000      4                 5
  46   Minivan        2000      3                 2.5;
  47   
  48   
  49  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  50  VARIABLES X(vehicles) vehicles manufactured (Number)
  51            VPROFIT  total profit ($);
  52   
  53  * Non-negativity constraints
  54  POSITIVE VARIABLES X;
  55   
  56  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  57  EQUATIONS
  58     PROFIT Total profit ($) and objective function value
  59     RES_CONSTRAIN(res) Resource Constraints;
  60   
  61  PROFIT..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(vehicles, c(vehicles)*X(vehicles));
  62  RES_CONSTRAIN(res) ..    SUM(vehicles, A(vehicles,res)*X(vehicles)) =L= b(res);
  63   
  64   
  65  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  66  MODEL PLANTING /PROFIT, RES_CONSTRAIN/;
  67  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  68  *MODEL PLANTING /ALL/;
  69   
  70   
  71  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  72  * Solve the PLANTING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  73  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  74  SOLVE PLANTING USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  75   
  76   
  77  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


